---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const title = 'About Proof to Partner | Evidence-Led B2B Introductions';
const description = 'Learn the purpose behind Proof to Partner: a practical, evidence-first approach to exploring commercial introductions across industries.';
const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }];
---
<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/about/" breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
<section class="bg-ink py-16 text-white sm:py-24"><div class="container-shell max-w-5xl"><p class="eyebrow !text-[#a4d4c7]">About Proof to Partner</p><h1 class="display-heading mt-6 max-w-4xl text-5xl font-semibold sm:text-6xl">Better connections begin with a clearer picture of the need.</h1><p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-white/70">Proof to Partner is being developed as a cross-industry B2B connector business. Its starting principle is straightforward: do the context work before asking people to spend time in a conversation.</p></div></section>
<section class="section-space"><div class="container-shell grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[.75fr_1.25fr] lg:gap-20"><div><p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p><h2 class="display-heading mt-5 text-4xl font-semibold">Less noise. More relevance.</h2></div><div class="space-y-5 text-base leading-8 text-muted"><p>Commercial introductions can be useful, but not when they start with guesswork. A company may be listed in the right category and still lack the availability, scope, coverage or interest to meet a particular requirement.</p><p>The aim is to connect a defined commercial need with research that considers those details. That may lead to a relevant introduction, a request for more information, or the conclusion that no suitable connection is available.</p><p>This website does not claim an established track record, a completed transaction history or a roster of verified partners. It explains the approach and gives buyers and suppliers a clear way to start a conversation.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="border-y border-line bg-white py-16"><div class="container-shell grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3"><article class="card-border p-6"><p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-brand">Principle 01</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">Evidence before assertion</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">Make the basis for a claim clear. Treat uncertain, stale or incomplete information as something to verify—not something to hide.</p></article><article class="card-border p-6"><p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-brand">Principle 02</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">Context over volume</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">A small number of relevant possibilities is more useful than a list assembled without a defined buyer-side need.</p></article><article class="card-border p-6"><p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-brand">Principle 03</p><h2 class="mt-4 text-xl font-semibold">Consent before connection</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">Parties should understand why an introduction is being proposed and agree to the next step before their information is shared.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="container-shell py-16 sm:py-20"><div class="max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">A developing business, with a defined approach</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-5">Proof to Partner is at an early stage. The focus is on building a clear process, being realistic about what can be established, and earning trust through useful conversations rather than making claims that have not yet been demonstrated.</p><a class="btn-primary mt-7" href="/contact/">Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
</SiteLayout>